    <section class="empire-glance" id="at-a-glance" aria-labelledby="glance-title">
      <div class="empire-glance-main"><h2 class="empire-glance-title" id="glance-title">At a glance</h2><ul><li>A Nubian kingdom on the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/nile">Nile</a> south of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/egypt">Egypt</a>, centred first at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/napata">Napata</a> and later at Meroe.</li><li>Its kings conquered <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/egypt">Egypt</a> and ruled it as the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/twenty-fifth-dynasty-of-egypt">Twenty-Fifth Dynasty</a>, then built an iron-working, pyramid-building civilisation at Meroe.</li><li>Shifting trade, environmental strain and pressure from <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/aksumite-empire">Aksum</a> ended Kush as a unified state by the mid-fourth century CE.</li></ul></div>
      <aside class="empire-dyk"><p class="empire-dyk-title">Did you know?</p><p>The Kushites built more pyramids, at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/el-kurru">El-Kurru</a>, Nuri and Meroe, than were built in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/egypt">Egypt</a> itself.</p></aside>
    </section>

